            <ArticleTitle>Successful management of a posterior saccular coronary artery aneurysm at the left main coronary artery bifurcation.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>37-9</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1111/j.1540-8191.2010.01030.x</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Left main coronary artery aneurysm is a rare condition that presents as a potential surgical challenge due to its location. We present a case of successful repair of a posterior saccular aneurysm of the left main coronary artery by aneurysm exclusion, afferent and efferent ligation with coronary artery bypass grafting.</AbstractText>
                <CopyrightInformation>© 2010 Wiley Periodicals, Inc.</CopyrightInformation>
            </Abstract>
